# OPTIONAL.
#
# The stack ships its own SQL Server, seeded from the checked-in bacpac at
# shesha-functional-tests/database/. You do NOT need this file to run it.
#
# Create `.env` from this template only if you want the instances to use a different database
# -- for example your own local SQL Server with data you care about.
#
# `.env` and any `.env.*` variant are gitignored. Never commit real credentials.

# --- Using your own local SQL Server -------------------------------------------------------
#
# Integrated Security cannot work from a Linux container, so SQL authentication is required:
#   1. Enable Mixed Mode authentication (SSMS -> Server Properties -> Security). Restart the service.
#   2. Enable TCP/IP on port 1433 (SQL Server Configuration Manager). Restart the service.
#   3. Add a Windows Firewall inbound rule for TCP 1433.
#
# `host.docker.internal` resolves to the Windows host from inside the containers.
#
# SHA_DB_CONNECTION=Data Source=host.docker.internal,1433;Initial Catalog=SheshaFunctionalTests;User Id=sa;Password=CHANGE_ME;TrustServerCertificate=True;Encrypt=False;
